      "finding": "Kunsch introduced block resampling for general stationary observations so local dependence is not destroyed by independent single-observation resampling.",
      "implementation_consequence": "Chronologically ordered capture-run uplift deltas are resampled in moving blocks rather than as independent trades."
    },
    {
      "source": "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4757-3803-2",
      "finding": "Lahiri documents block-bootstrap methods for inference on dependent temporal data and the importance of block-size choice.",
      "implementation_consequence": "The predeclared shared resampler uses a bounded square-root run block length and reports that length with every result."
    },
    {
      "source": "https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/prc/section4/prc473.htm",
      "finding": "Bonferroni simultaneous intervals retain at least the requested overall confidence when each of g preselected intervals uses confidence one minus alpha divided by g.",
      "implementation_consequence": "Two pinned AI reviewers each use a 97.5 percent interval so the family of two has at least 95 percent simultaneous coverage."
    },
    {
      "source": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.3982/ecta5771",
      "finding": "Comparing multiple predictive models without accounting for selection uncertainty can admit spurious winners.",
      "implementation_consequence": "Neither AI reviewer qualifies unless its own dependence-aware lower uplift bound is strictly positive; no best-reviewer selection occurs in development."
    }
  ],
